# --- Maps (the `rides` store package surface) ---
# LEAVE ALL THREE UNSET and the Rides map still works: the default is a real slippy map
# over keyless OpenStreetMap tiles with Leaflet vendored into the package. No account,
# no billing, no partner registration.
# Set GOOGLE_MAPS_BROWSER_KEY to upgrade that same surface to Google Maps — you get a
# road-routed polyline (Directions) and Places autocomplete instead of a straight line and
# Nominatim search. Needs a BILLING-ENABLED key from a Google Cloud project registered
# under the business email (docs/partner-app-registration.md), with Maps JavaScript API +
# Places API + Directions API enabled. It is a BROWSER key — it ships to the page, so
# restrict it by HTTP referrer in the Cloud console and never reuse a server-side key here.
# GOOGLE_MAPS_BROWSER_KEY=
# GOOGLE_MAPS_MAP_ID=                # optional Cloud-styled map id
# OSHAL_MAP_TILE_URL=                # optional: your own {s}/{z}/{x}/{y} tile server for the OSM path

# --- Jira ---
# CONNECTOR_JIRA_BASE_URL=           # falls back to JIRA_BASE_URL

# --- Telegram (inbound chat channel) ---
